{"description":"A round of polish ahead of the release: a clearer fetch/download split, consistent domain language across the CLI and wire protocol, plus display and refactor cleanups.\n\n## CLI behaviour\n\n- Split `fetch` (warm the store only) from `download` (export to disk), each with its own receipt; add `download --offline` to export complete bytes without touching the network\n- Allow `fetch`/`download` with `--cid` alone, picking the most recently created release as primary\n- Make `unseed` take `--cid` as a flag, matching every other command\n- Resolve fetch output paths against the CLI cwd, not the daemon's\n- Mark artifacts we serve with a 🌱 in `list` and `show`, derived locally from the COB with no node RPC\n\n## Language\n\n- Reserve \"register\" for Artifacts and Locations; \"create\" for a Release; \"tag\" for the local store operation\n- Speak Location (ours), not provider (iroh's), across the wire protocol and CLI; confine provider to the fetch layer\n- Use add/remove for Locations; disambiguate Seeder from a Radicle seed node\n- Define Fetch, Download, and Temp Tag in CONTEXT.md\n- Rename register output's `revision` to `oid` for consistency with list and show\n\n## Refactors\n\n- Centralize FetchProgress rendering behind an exhaustive, unit-tested mapping\n- Extract `run_blocking`, `log_retrieval_plan`, and `EndpointId::matches_url` helpers\n- Add a `make check` target running fmt and clippy","revision":"9a0a5773c4b624f2e004b6f58875f6de3b64f1aa","type":"revision.edit"}